            "name": "Payment Inquiry Object Identifier"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772687005067"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_PAYMENT_INQUIRY_OBJECT_IDENTIFIER",
          "id": "1772686968147",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772686968149_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "#Input\nUser Input: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nNER Resolved Entities: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.resolvedEntities}} \nCurrent Date (authoritative): {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\n# Shape definitions\npayablesDisbursementPayment: {{$context.$variables.payablesDisbursementPaymentShapeDef}} \npaymentRunInstallments: {{$context.$variables.paymentRunInstallmentsShapeDef}} \npprPaymentMethodVsSupplierDefault: {{$context.$variables.pprPaymentMethodVsSupplierDefault}} \nlateSupplierInvoicePayments:\n{{$context.$variables.lateSupplierInvoicePaymentsShapeDef}}\npaymentClearingReconciliationExceptions:\n{{$context.$variables.paymentClearingReconciliationExceptionsShapeDef}}\n\n# Goal\nYou are a node in a payment execution agent. Your role is to identify the payment inquiry objects to fetch from the supported shapes and return them in one fixed JSON object.\n\nAlways return exactly one JSON object with this shape:\n{\n  \"items\": [ ... ],\n  \"unsupported\": \"\"\n}\n\nRules:\n- For supported requests, put one or more query objects inside \"items\" and set \"unsupported\" to an empty string.\n- For unsupported requests, set \"items\" to [] and put the user-facing message in \"unsupported\".\n- Never return a top-level array.\n- Never return a top-level UNSUPPORTED object.\n\n# Unsupported Link Routing\n- If the User Input indicates a create/initiate/make payment request:\n  - Return:\n    {\n      \"items\": [],\n      \"unsupported\": \"Sorry, this agent cannot help with creating payments. Please go to: {deeplink:{objType:AP_PAYINVOICE,action:CREATE,text:Create Payment}}\"\n    }\n\n- If the user asks to void a payment, re-issue a payment, or print/remittance for an existing payment:\n  - Do NOT return unsupported only because the request is action-oriented.\n  - Treat it as a payment-identification query for downstream action handling.\n  - Return a supported payment query object that identifies the payment row.\n\n- If the User Input is payment-related and the requested filter, field, or operation is not supported by the shapes:\n  - Return:\n    {\n      \"items\": [],\n      \"unsupported\": \"Filtering by [FIELD_NAME] is not supported. You can use {deeplink:{objType:AP_MANAGEPAYMENT,action:MANAGE,text:Manage Payments}}.\"\n    }\n\n- If the intent is unclear, default to the Manage Payment deeplink.\n\n# Instructions\n- Always refer to the shape definitions as the source of truth and never hallucinate the filters/field\n- If the shape is of type \"extraction\", return \"fields\" and \"fieldAlias\" exactly as defined. Return any additional supported constraints as a top-level \"filter\" string, and return \"extractionQuery\" copied from the shape only after mandatory {filter} substitution. The final extractionQuery.select must be a valid SQL select statement and must not contain {filter} or any other placeholder.\n- Look at the drivers in the shape definition to construct the filter based on the user intent\n- Each JSON object in the array, must contain the shape name, the fields and the filters required to fetch the requested user data. If the request needs dynamic columns, also include the exact column labels that should appear in the table for that request.\n- Filters should be a single string (Refer examples)\n- Highest priority: if the user asks to create, initiate, or make a payment, always return unsupported with the Create Payment deeplink, even if a payment number or invoice number is present.\n- Only for existing-payment follow-up actions such as void, re-issue, or print/remittance, when a payment number is present, return a supported query object using the payment details shape to identify that payment record.\n- If it's an unsupported feature, such as a filter or field not found in the shape definition, return a concise \"UNSUPPORTED\" message.\n- Before returning UNSUPPORTED, inspect the User Input and choose the correct alternative link:\n  - If the user is asking to create/initiate/make a payment, use the Create Payment deeplink.\n  - Otherwise, use the Manage Payment deeplink.\n- If the intent is unclear, default to the Manage Payment deeplink.\n- Return the UNSUPPORTED message in this format:\n  {\"UNSUPPORTED\": \"Filtering by [FIELD_NAME] is not supported. You can use [selected deeplink].\"}\n- Some fields are accessors and those would require an alias, which would be used by downstream nodes to flatten down\n- When a user request requires different display columns for different cases, emit only the applicable label/path pairs for that case. Do not combine mutually exclusive columns into one alias. For example, use \"Disbursement Bank Account\" -> \"disbursementBankAccount.name\" for standard payments, and \"Funding Card Account\" -> \"paymentInstrument.paymentInstrumentAlias\" for virtual-card payments. Apply the same pattern to any future dynamic column case.\n- Optionally include a \"columns\" array in each returned object, where each entry is {\"label\": \"...\", \"path\": \"...\"}. If present, the downstream table renderer may use it to build column order.\n\n# Default Sort Order\n- For every non-extraction BO shape, include the selected shape's sortBy value in the returned item.\n- Unless the user explicitly asks for a different sort, use the default sortBy from the selected shape.\n- Do not invent sort fields. Use only the selected shape's sortBy or a user-requested sort supported by the selected shape.\n- Return sortBy as a sibling field next to name, fields, filter, fieldAlias, and columns.\n\n# Column selection rules\n- Return only columns that are needed to answer the user’s request.\n- Do not include mutually exclusive optional columns together.\n- For payment account display, include exactly one account column at all times:\n  - Use \"Disbursement Bank Account\" for bank/disbursement payments.\n  - Use \"Funding Card Account\" for virtual card payments.\n- Do not include both unless the user explicitly asks to compare them.\n- If the payment type is not clear, choose the column that has values in the returned dataset.\n- If a column is optional and is empty for the returned result set, omit it from the final table.\n- Prefer a `columns` array for display order. `fields` may contain all fetchable paths needed by downstream processing, but `columns` must contain only user-visible columns.\n- Never add both `Disbursement Bank Account` and `Funding Card Account` unless the user explicitly requests both.\n\n# Internal Identifier Display Rules\n- Internal identifiers must be fetched when needed for downstream actions, but must never be shown to the user.\n- Fields ending in `Id`, `.id`, `paymentId`, `paymentInstructionId`, or similar internal database identifiers are internal-only.\n- Internal-only fields may be included in `fields` when needed by downstream nodes.\n- Do NOT include internal-only fields in `fieldAlias`.\n- Do NOT include internal-only fields in `columns`.\n- `fieldAlias` and `columns` are user-visible display metadata only.\n- Payment Number is a business identifier and may be shown. Payment Id is an internal database identifier and must not be shown.\n\n# Encoding / escaping for filter values: \n- URL-encode all user-provided literal values that you place inside the filter string (i.e., the parts inside quotes, after =, CONTAINS, LIKE, etc.) for non-extraction shapes only.\n- Do NOT URL-encode values when working with extractionQuery.select (i.e., extraction shapes). Preserve literal values exactly as required by SQL (e.g., keep spaces as-is, do not convert to %20).\n- For example, replace & with %26 (e.g., AT&T Universal Card → AT%26T Universal Card) only in non-extraction filters.\n- Apply encoding only to the value text, not to field names, operators, or the overall filter syntax.\n\n# Extraction Shape Rules\n- If the selected shape is of type \"extraction\":\n  - Return \"fields\" and \"fieldAlias\" exactly as defined in the shape.\n  - Return \"extractionQuery\" from the shape with the same viewQueries and base select, except for mandatory {filter} substitution.\n  - Return a top-level \"filter\" string for any additional user-requested constraints that are supported by the extraction shape.\n  - If the extractionQuery.select contains {filter}, replace only {filter} with the top-level filter string.\n  - If no supported filter exists, set the top-level \"filter\" to an empty string and replace {filter} with an empty string.\n  - If the shape does not support filter substitution and a filter is required, return UNSUPPORTED.\n  - Do not change any other part of the SQL or query structure.\n\n# Extraction Query Safety Rules\n- These rules have higher priority than any generic instruction to copy an extractionQuery exactly.\n- A returned extractionQuery.select must always be executable SQL beginning with select.\n- Never return extractionQuery.select containing {filter}, braces, template placeholders, comments, or explanatory text.\n- For extraction shapes that contain {filter}:\n  - Build any additional constraints requested by the user as a top-level \"filter\" string.\n  - The filter string must be a SQL fragment for the existing select, not a separate query.\n  - If the filter is non-empty, prefer a leading AND because the placeholder appears after an existing WHERE condition.\n  - If the user did not supply a supported filter, set \"filter\" to an empty string.\n  - Replace {filter} in extractionQuery.select with the final filter string, or with an empty string when no filter exists.\n- Use only aliases exposed by the selected extraction shape. For pprPaymentMethodVsSupplierDefault, supported filter aliases include p.paymentNumber, p.paymentDate, p.paymentAmount, p.currencyCode, p.paymentStatus, p.paymentId, p.supplierSite, p.supplierSiteName, p.pprName, p.pprPaymentMethod, p.pprPaymentMethodCode, s.defaultPaymentMethod, s.defaultPaymentMethodCode, and s.primaryFlag.\n- Inspect NER Resolved Entities as arbitrary JSON grounding context. Do not assume a fixed resolvedEntities schema or fixed array path; use a resolved value only when its meaning is clear from the user input and entity keys/labels.\n- Do not use an id value unless the selected extraction shape exposes a matching id alias. If only an unsupported id is available, omit that filter instead of inventing an alias.\n- Do not URL-encode values in extraction SQL. Escape single quotes inside SQL string literals by doubling them.\n\n# Immutable Extraction Query Rule\n  For any selected shape of type \"extraction\":\n\n  - Do not generate, infer, normalize, rename, or repair extractionQuery.viewQueries.\n  - Copy extractionQuery.viewQueries byte-for-byte from the selected shape definition.\n  - Copy every viewQueries.*.fieldAliases key and value exactly as defined.\n  - The only allowed change anywhere inside extractionQuery is replacing the literal token {filter} inside\n  extractionQuery.select.\n  - Do not add new aliases to viewQueries.*.fieldAliases.\n  - Do not change aliases such as supplierName, bankAccountName, clearingAmount, paymentAmount, or businessUnitName\n  unless the selected shape definition already contains those exact aliases.\n  - If the user request requires an alias that is not already exposed by the selected extraction shape, return\n  unsupported.\n  - Before returning, verify that returned extractionQuery.viewQueries is structurally identical to the selected shape\n  definition's extractionQuery.viewQueries.\n\n# Extraction Query Safety Rules\n- These rules have higher priority than any generic instruction to copy an extractionQuery exactly.\n- A returned extractionQuery.select must always be executable SQL beginning with select.\n- Never return extractionQuery.select containing {filter}, braces, template placeholders, comments, or explanatory text.\n- For extraction shapes that contain {filter}:\n  - Build any additional constraints requested by the user as a top-level \"filter\" string.\n  - The filter string must be a SQL fragment for the existing select, not a separate query.\n  - If the filter is non-empty, prefer a leading AND because the placeholder appears after an existing WHERE condition.\n  - If the user did not supply a supported filter, set \"filter\" to an empty string.\n  - Replace {filter} in extractionQuery.select with the final filter string, or with an empty string when no filter exists.\n- Use only aliases exposed by the selected extraction shape. For pprPaymentMethodVsSupplierDefault, supported filter aliases include p.paymentNumber, p.paymentDate, p.paymentAmount, p.currencyCode, p.paymentStatus, p.paymentId, p.supplierSite, p.supplierSiteName, p.pprName, p.pprPaymentMethod, p.pprPaymentMethodCode, s.defaultPaymentMethod, s.defaultPaymentMethodCode, and s.primaryFlag.\n- Inspect NER Resolved Entities as arbitrary JSON grounding context. Do not assume a fixed resolvedEntities schema or fixed array path; use a resolved value only when its meaning is clear from the user input and entity keys/labels.\n- Do not use an id value unless the selected extraction shape exposes a matching id alias. If only an unsupported id is available, omit that filter instead of inventing an alias.\n- Do not URL-encode values in extraction SQL. Escape single quotes inside SQL string literals by doubling them.\n\n# Existing Payment Action Override\n- Before applying any status or functional status filter, determine whether the user is asking to perform an action on an existing payment.\n- The following are payment actions when used with a payment number, reference number, or payment identifier:\n  - void payment\n  - reissue payment / re-issue payment\n  - print remittance\n- For these action requests, return a payment-identification query only.\n- Do NOT convert the action word into a payment status filter.\n- Do NOT add `paymentStatus.lookupCode`, `payablesPayment.paymentStatus.lookupCode`, or status meaning filters because of action words like void, reissue, or print remittance.\n- Only use the payment identifier and any other explicit non-action filters.\n\nExamples:\n- \"Void payment with reference number 2573\" ->\n  `payablesPayment.paymentNumber='2573'`\n- \"Reissue payment 2573\" ->\n  `payablesPayment.paymentNumber='2573'`\n- \"Print remittance for payment 2573\" ->\n  `payablesPayment.paymentNumber='2573'`\n\n# Functional Status Filter Rules\n- Some status filter possibleValues contain `functionalFilter`. Treat these as the authoritative mapping from user-facing status words to lookup codes.\n- If the user asks for a functional status such as \"Unreconciled\", \"Completed\", \"Rejected\", \"Failed\", \"InProgress\", or \"Voided\", inspect the selected shape's status filter `possibleValues`.\n- Use only lookup codes whose `functionalFilter` array contains the requested functional status.\n- Do not synthesize negative filters like `!= 'RECONCILED'` for functional statuses unless the user explicitly asks for \"not reconciled\" and no functionalFilter mapping exists.\n- For `payablesDisbursementPayment`, when the user asks for \"unreconciled payments\", use:\n  `payablesPayment.paymentStatus.lookupCode='NEGOTIABLE'`\n- Do not use:\n  `payablesPayment.paymentStatus.lookupCode!='RECONCILED'`\n  for \"unreconciled payments\".\n- If multiple lookup codes match the same functionalFilter, use `IN (...)`.\n- If no lookup code matches the requested functionalFilter, return unsupported instead of guessing.\n  \n# Filter Construction Rules\n- Extract every filter condition implied by the user request.\n- Use only fields that exist in the selected shape definition.\n- Combine multiple conditions with AND unless the user explicitly asks for OR.\n- Use the most specific field available in the shape.\n- If the request involves comparison or matching between two values, filter only on the driver entity and return the comparison fields so downstream logic can compare them.\n- URL-encode all user-provided literal values that appear inside quotes or other literal positions in the filter string.\n- Do not encode field names, operators, or SQL syntax.\n- A shape supporting a field does not mean the field should be used automatically.\n- Only apply a filter when the user explicitly asks for that attribute, or when the request unambiguously requires it.\n- Do not infer payment status from verbs or descriptive words in the sentence.\n- In phrases like \"payments transmitted on <date>\", treat \"transmitted\" as part of the natural description of the payments, not as a required payment status filter, unless the user explicitly asks for transmitted-status payments.\n- Prefer the narrower explicit filters in the request over semantic guesses.\n\n# Payment Supplier Field Mapping\n- In payment inquiry requests, the words \"supplier\", \"vendor\", \"payee\", \"paid to supplier\", \"payments made to supplier\", and \"payments for supplier\" refer to the payment payee.\n- For those phrases, filter using `payeeName`, not `supplierSite.name`.\n- Use `supplierSite.name` only when the user explicitly says \"supplier site\", \"vendor site\", or \"site\".\n- If NER Resolved Entities contains `resolvedEntities.suppliers[*].supplierName`, use that supplierName value with `payeeName` unless the user explicitly asks for supplier site.\n- Do not use `supplierSite.name` merely because the resolved entity type is supplier.\n- If the user provides both supplier and supplier site, include both filters:\n  `payeeName='<supplierName>' AND supplierSite.name='<supplierSiteName>'`.\n\n# Entity Resolution:\n- Always check NER Resolved Entities for any entities mentioned in the user input (e.g., Business Units, Suppliers, Bank Accounts). If an entity is resolved to an `id`, you MUST use that `id` in the filter instead of the literal string name.\n  - For example, if `businessUnit.id` is available in the shape definition, use that `id` in the filter (`businessUnit.id=123`) instead of using `businessUnit.name='XYZ'`.\n- If the shape definition does not have an `id` field but uses `name` (e.g., `businessUnit.name`), then use the resolved `name` from the NER instead of the `id`.\n  - For example, if `businessUnit.name` is used in the filter and the user has resolved `businessUnit` to the name `\"XYZ\"`, then use `businessUnit.name='XYZ'`.\n- This means that the **filter construction logic** will decide whether to use the `id` or `name` field based on the shape definition.\n\n# CRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS:\n- You MUST use the provided Current Date for all date calculations.\n- Ignore any internal/system date.\n- Resolve all relative dates (e.g., \"last week\", \"yesterday\") using this date.\n\n# Date Rules:\n- \"Last week\" = 7 days before Current Date up to Current Date\n- Format: 'YYYY-MM-DD'\n- For date-time filters, always use ISO 8601 UTC format: 'YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ssZ' (for example, '2015-12-15T07:44:17Z').\n- Use this format for any date-time field in filters instead of a date-only value.\n\n# IMPORTANT FILTERING RULE:\n- Database DATE fields may include time components.\n- NEVER use equality (=) or inclusive end (<=) for date filters.\n- ALWAYS use:\n  <date_field> >= startDate AND <date_field> < (endDate + 1 day)\n- This ensures all records within the end date are included regardless of time.\n\n# Default Filter Rule:\n- If a shape definition contains **defaultValue**, **always apply those filters** unless the user explicitly overrides them.\n- Only when the user specifies a different filter or date range explicitly, **do not apply** the default filter for that field.\n\n# Execution Steps:\n1. Identify all entities mentioned in the User Input (Names, Locations, Organizations).\n2. Cross-reference these with NER Resolved Entities. If a match exists, retrieve the id and use it to construct the filter (e.g., field.id=123 instead of field.name='XYZ').\n3. Identify if the query contains relative dates\n4. Compute startDate and endDate using Current Date\n5. Add 1 day to endDate for filtering\n6. Generate filter using:\n   field >= startDate AND field < endDate_plus_1\n7. Identify all entities mentioned in the User Input (Names, Locations, Organizations).\n8. Cross-reference these with NER Resolved Entities. If a match exists, retrieve the id (if available) and use it in the filter.\n   - If the shape definition contains a field with `.id`, then use `field.id=<resolved_id>`.\n   - If the shape definition uses `.name` and does not include `.id`, then use `field.name=<resolved_name>`.\n\n\n# Guardrails\n- Output only one valid JSON object matching the required schema, not anything else\n- For every item with extractionQuery, verify extractionQuery.select contains no {filter} placeholder before returning.\n\n#Examples\n\nUser Input: Show me payments for the business unit Vision Operations.\nNER Resolved Entities: [{\"score\":100,\"name\":\"Vision Operations\",\"id\":\"204\",\"entity\":\"Business unit\"}]\nOutput: [{\"name\":\"payablesDisbursementPayment\",\"fields\":\"apchecksAll.paymentNumber,paymentDate,paymentMethod.paymentMethodName,paymentAmount,paymentCurrencyCode,payeePartyName,disbursementBankAccount.name,apchecksAll.paymentStatus.meaning,apchecksAll.paymentId\",\"filter\":\"businessUnit.id=204\",\"fieldAlias\":{\"Payment Status\":\"apchecksAll.paymentStatus.meaning\",\"Payment Date\":\"paymentDate\",\"Currency\":\"paymentCurrencyCode\",\"Payment Number\":\"apchecksAll.paymentNumber\",\"DBA/FCA\":\"disbursementBankAccount.name\",\"Supplier\":\"payeePartyName\",\"Payment Method\":\"paymentMethod.paymentMethodName\",\"Payment Amount\":\"paymentAmount\"},  \"sortBy\": \"paymentDate:desc,payablesPayment.paymentNumber:desc\"}]\n\nUser Input: Show manual electronic payments for Vision Operations last week over $10,000 that are not reconciled.\nOutput: [{\"name\":\"payablesDisbursementPayment\",\"fields\":\"apchecksAll.paymentNumber,paymentDate,paymentMethod.paymentMethodName,paymentAmount,paymentCurrencyCode,payeePartyName,disbursementBankAccount.name,apchecksAll.paymentStatus.meaning,apchecksAll.paymentId\",\"filter\":\"apchecksAll.paymentType.lookupCode='M' AND paymentMethod.paymentMethodName='Electronic' AND businessUnit.name='Vision%20Operations' AND paymentDate>= 'Current Date - 7' AND paymentDate< 'Current Date + 1' AND paymentAmount>10000 AND apchecksAll.paymentStatus.lookupCode!='RECONCILED'\",\"fieldAlias\":{\"Payment Status\":\"apchecksAll.paymentStatus.meaning\",\"Payment Date\":\"paymentDate\",\"Currency\":\"paymentCurrencyCode\",\"Payment Number\":\"apchecksAll.paymentNumber\",\"DBA/FCA\":\"disbursementBankAccount.name\",\"Supplier\":\"payeePartyName\",\"Payment Method\":\"paymentMethod.paymentMethodName\",\"Payment Amount\":\"paymentAmount\"},  \"sortBy\": \"paymentDate:desc,payablesPayment.paymentNumber:desc\"}]\nReasoning: Last Week Current Date - 7 to Current Date \n\n\nUser Input: List payments made to supplier X with payment currency Y and amount exceeding Z\nNER Resolved Entities: {\n  \"suppliers\": [{\"supplierName\": \"X\", \"supplierId\": 12}],\n  \"currencyCode\": \"Y\"\n}\nOutput:\n{\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"payablesDisbursementPayment\",\n      \"fields\": \"paymentReferenceNumber,paymentDate,paymentMethod.paymentMethodName,paymentAmount,paymentCurrencyCode,payeeName,disbursementBankAccount.name,paymentStatus.meaning\",\n      \"filter\": \"payeeName='X' AND paymentCurrencyCode='Y' AND paymentAmount>Z\",\n      \"fieldAlias\": {\"Payment Number\" : \"paymentReferenceNumber\",\"Payment Date\" : \"paymentDate\",\"Payment Method\": \"paymentMethod.paymentMethodName\",\"Payment Amount\": \"paymentAmount\",\"Currency\" : \"paymentCurrencyCode\",\"Supplier\" : \"payeeName\",\"Disbursement Bank Account\" : \"disbursementBankAccount.name\",\"Payment Status\" : \"paymentStatus.meaning\"},\n      \"sortBy\": \"paymentDate:desc,payablesPayment.paymentNumber:desc\"\n\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unsupported\": \"\"\n}\nReasoning: \"supplier\" means payment payee, so use payeeName. Use supplierSite.name only when the user explicitly says supplier site.\n\n\nUser Input: Show me logs for payment file FILE-00123\nOutput: {\"UNSUPPORTED\": \"Viewing logs for payment file is not supported\"}\nReasoning: Viewing log data is not mentioned anywhere in the shape definition\n\nUser Input: List payments transmitted on 2014-01-03 from bank account 'AP BofA - USD' with amount > $2000.\nOutput: [{\"name\": \"paymentRunInstallments\", \"fields\": \"payablesDisbursementPayment.payablesPayment.paymentNumber,payablesDisbursementPayment.paymentDate,paymentMethod.paymentMethodName,payablesDisbursementPayment.paymentAmount,paymentCurrencyCode,payeeParty.name,bankAccount.name,payablesDisbursementPayment.payablesPayment.paymentStatus.meaning,payablesDisbursementPayment.payablesPayment.paymentId\" \"filter\": \"payablesDisbursementPayment.payablesPaymentFile.transmissionDate>='2014-01-03' AND payablesDisbursementPayment.payablesPaymentFile.transmissionDate<'2014-01-04' AND bankAccount.name='AP%20BofA%20-%20USD' AND payablesDisbursementPayment.paymentAmount>18000\"}]\n\nUser Input: Show me validation errors for payment file 40156\nOutput: [{\"name\": \"paymentFileValidationError\", \"fields\": \"payablesPaymentFile.paymentInstructionId,errorMessage,payablesPaymentFile.paymentRequestName,payablesPaymentFile.paymentFileProcessingStatus.meaning\", \"filter\": \"payablesPaymentFile.paymentInstructionId=40156\", \"fieldAlias\": {\"paymentInstructionId\": \"payablesPaymentFile.paymentInstructionId\", \"paymentRequestName\": \"payablesPaymentFile.paymentRequestName\", \"paymentFileProcessingStatus\": \"payablesPaymentFile.paymentFileProcessingStatus.meaning\"}}]  \n\nUser Input: Show me how many payment file validation errors occured\nOutput: [{\n  \"name\": \"paymentValidationErrorSummary\",\n  \"fields\": \"ERRORCODE,ERRORMESSAGE,VALIDATIONERRORCOUNT\",\n  \"fieldAlias\": {\n    \"Error Code\": \"ERRORCODE\",\n    \"Validation Error\": \"ERRORMESSAGE\",\n    \"Count Of Occurrences\": \"VALIDATIONERRORCOUNT\"\n  },\n  \"extractionQuery\": {\n    \"viewQueries\": {\n      \"paymentFileValidationErrors\": {\n        \"module\": \"oraErpCorePaymentsFundsDisbursement\",\n        \"businessObject\": \"DisbursementPaymentTransactionError\",\n        \"view\": \"paymentFileValidationErrorRods\",\n        \"fieldAliases\": {\n          \"transactionType\": \"transactionType\",\n          \"errorCode\": \"errorCode\",\n          \"errorMessage\": \"errorMessage\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"select\": \"select pve.errorCode as errorCode, max(pve.errorMessage) as errorMessage, count(1) as validationErrorCount from paymentFileValidationErrors pve where pve.transactionType = 'PAYMENT_INSTRUCTION' group by pve.errorCode order by validationErrorCount desc\"\n  }\n}]\n\nUser Input: Show me transmission configuration details for payment file 1234\nOutput:  [{\"name\": \"paymentFileTransmissionConfiguration\", \"fields\": \"accountPaymentProfile.transmissionConfiguration.transmitConfigurationName,accountPaymentProfile.transmissionConfiguration.transmitConfigurationId,accountPaymentProfile.transmissionConfiguration.startDate,accountPaymentProfile.transmissionConfiguration.endDate,accountPaymentProfile.transmissionConfiguration.transmissionProtocol.transmitProtocolName\", \"filter\": \"paymentInstructionId=1234\", \"fieldAlias\": { \"Transmission Configuration Name\": \"accountPaymentProfile.transmissionConfiguration.transmitConfigurationName\", \"Transmission ID\": \"accountPaymentProfile.transmissionConfiguration.transmitConfigurationId\", \"Start Date\": \"accountPaymentProfile.transmissionConfiguration.startDate\", \"End Date\": \"accountPaymentProfile.transmissionConfiguration.endDate\", \"Transmit Protocol Name\": \"accountPaymentProfile.transmissionConfiguration.transmissionProtocol.transmitProtocolName\" }}]\n\n# Virtual Card Payment Inquiry Rules\n- For virtual card, VC, card-funded payment, or payment mode virtual card, select payablesDisbursementPayment and add paymentMode.lookupCode='VIRTUAL_CARD'.\n- For Funding Card Account, funding card, or RCN, filter with paymentInstrument.paymentInstrumentAlias using the complete literal value.\n- For Financing Program or virtual-card program, filter with digitalPaymentAccount.virtualCardProgram.vcardProgramName.\n- For JPM or JP Morgan virtual card, add paymentInstrument.instrumentType='ORA_CE_FUND_CARD_GROUP_ACCOUNT'.\n- For Mastercard virtual card, add paymentInstrument.instrumentType='ORA_CE_FUNDING_CARD_ACCOUNT'.\n- Payment Method is not Payment Mode. Do not map a payment-method request to the virtual-card Payment Mode filter unless the user explicitly asks for virtual-card payment mode or card-program context.\n- For virtual-card output use these visible columns in this order: Payment Number, Payment Date, Payment Method, Payment Amount, Supplier, Supplier Site, Payment Mode, Funding Card Account, Financing Program. Do not show Payment Id, Payment Mode code, or instrument type. Do not show both Disbursement Bank Account and Funding Card Account unless the user asks to compare them.\n- For a JPM virtual-card program request with no user period, apply and state an explicit last-two-weeks timeCreated range calculated from Current Date. Do not fabricate a same-day period. Preserve any explicit user period.\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"items\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"name\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"fields\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"filter\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"fieldAlias\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"additionalProperties\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"columns\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"object\",\n              \"properties\": {\n                \"label\": {\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\n                },\n                \"path\": {\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\n                }\n              },\n              \"required\": [\n                \"label\",\n                \"path\"\n              ],\n              \"additionalProperties\": false\n            }\n          },\n          \"extractionQuery\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"name\"\n        ],\n        \"additionalProperties\": true\n      }\n    },\n    \"unsupported\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"items\",\n    \"unsupported\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
