        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Payment Inquiry data summarizer"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772687266593"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_PAYMENT_INQUIRY_DATA_SUMMARIZER",
          "id": "1772687229139",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772687229140_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Input\nUser Input: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}  \nData fetched: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_FOR_PAYMENT_INQUIRY_OBJECT_FETCH_LOOP.$output}}  \nApplied Filters Array: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_PAYMENT_INQUIRY_OBJECT_IDENTIFIER.$output.items}}  \nRecord Limit: {{$context.$variables.hasMore}}  \n\n# Goal\nGenerate a concise, natural, and agentic **summary** of the fetched data and provide **recommendations** for the user based on available links and the user query.\n\n# Instructions\n\n## Part 1: Generate Summary\n\n1. Determine the number of records retrieved from `{{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_FOR_PAYMENT_INQUIRY_OBJECT_FETCH_LOOP.$output}}`.\n\n2. Identify relevant filters:\n   - Each object in \"Applied Filters Array\" contains a \"filter\" field.\n   - Select ONLY the filter(s) relevant to the user query and fetched data.\n   - Ignore unrelated filters.\n\n3. Convert selected filter(s) into natural language:\n   - Do NOT use symbols like \"=\", \"<\", \">\", etc.\n   - Translate operators into readable words:\n       - \"=\" → \"is\"\n       - \"<\" → \"before\"\n       - \">\" → \"after\"\n   - Remove technical prefixes (e.g., \"apchecksAll.\")\n   - Convert field names into readable terms (e.g., \"paymentNumber\" → \"payment number\")\n   - Convert values into clean format (e.g., dates like \"2026-02-26\" → \"Feb 26, 2026\")\n   - Combine multiple filters into a smooth phrase using \"and\"\n\n   Example:  \n   Input: \"apchecksAll.paymentStatus='NEGOTIABLE' AND apchecksAll.paymentDate < '2026-02-26'\"  \n   Output: \"with status negotiable and payment dates before Feb 26, 2026\"\n\n4. Generate the summary sentence based on the number of records:\n   - If NO records are found:  \n     → \"I couldn’t find any payment records <natural language filters>.\"\n   - If ONLY ONE record is found:  \n     → \"I found 1 payment record for your selected criteria.\"\n   - Multiple records:  \n     → If Records Limit is true:  \n       \"I found multiple payment records <natural language filters>. Showing only the first 20 records.\"  \n     → If Records Limit is false:  \n       \"I found <X> payment records <natural language filters>.\"\n   \n5. **Extract insightful data** from `{{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_FOR_PAYMENT_INQUIRY_OBJECT_FETCH_LOOP.$output}}`:\n- This part should only be used if there are **multiple records**. If there is only one record, **skip** the detailed insights.\n   - Highlight key points such as:\n     - **Trends**: For example, \"Many of the payments have been processed within the last 30 days.\"\n     - **Payment Sizes**: \"The average payment amount is $X, with the highest payment being $Y.\"\n     - **Outstanding Amounts**: \"A significant portion of payments still have outstanding balances.\"\n     - **Payment Issues**: \"Several payments are overdue by more than 10 days.\"\n     - **Recent Activity**: \"The most recent payment was processed on [specific date].\"\n     - **Patterns**: \"Most records are associated with [particular payment method/department].\"\n\n   - Make sure the summary captures the most relevant and actionable insights that a user might find valuable based on the context of their query and the fetched data. It should focus on patterns, outliers, or significant figures.\n\n6. Keep the summary:\n   - Concise and natural\n   - Agentic (\"I found...\", \"I couldn’t find...\")\n   - Easy for non-technical users to understand\n\n## Part 2: Generate Recommendations\n 1. **Check if Data fetched is empty**:\n- If `Data fetched` contains no data (i.e., no records), return **empty recommendations** or **empty string** for recommendations.\n2. Check the **Data fetched** for the presence of any links (`deepLinks` or `relativeLinks` fields).\n3. Analyze the user query:\n- If the query mentions actions like **\"void\"**, **\"reissue\"**, or **\"print remittance\"**, **prioritize these actions** in the recommendation.\n- Otherwise, provide a general recommendation for reviewing details.\n4. **Recommendation rules**:\n- **If links exist in the fetched data and the user query mentions voiding**: \n  → **Check if additional details (e.g., invoice action) are provided**:\n    - If additional details are provided (e.g., \"Place hold on Invoice\"):  \n      \"<b>Suggestions:</b><br>Use the links in the table to navigate to the payment page. From there, select the ‘Void’ option from the action dropdown and apply the necessary details (e.g., 'Place hold on Invoice').\"\n    - If no additional details are provided:  \n      \"<b>Suggestions:</b><br>Use the links in the table to navigate to the payment page and void the payment.\"\n\n- **If links exist in the fetched data and the user query mentions reissuing**:  \n  → **Check if additional details (e.g., invoice action) are provided**:\n    - If additional details are provided:  \n      \"<b>Suggestions:</b><br>Use the links in the table to navigate to the payment page. From there, select the ‘Reissue’ option from the action dropdown and apply the necessary details (e.g., 'Reissue payment for Invoice 123').\"\n    - If no additional details are provided:  \n      \"<b>Suggestions:</b><br>Use the links in the table to navigate to the payment page and reissue the payment.\"\n\n- **If links exist in the fetched data and the user query mentions printing remittance**:  \n  → **Check if additional details are provided**:\n    - If additional details are provided:  \n      \"<b>Suggestions:</b><br>Use the links in the table to navigate to the payment page. From there, select the ‘Reprint Remittance’ option from the action dropdown and apply the necessary details.\"\n    - If no additional details are provided:  \n      \"<b>Suggestions:</b><br>Use the links in the table to navigate to the payment page and print the remittance.\"\n\n- **If links exist and the user query is general** (not related to voiding, reissuing, or printing remittance):  \n  → \"<b>Suggestions:</b><br>Use the links in the table to review details and take appropriate actions.\"\n\n- **If no links exist**:  \n  → \"<b>Suggestions:</b><br>No actionable links available in the fetched data.\"\n5. Preserve HTML formatting:\n- Do NOT escape or modify HTML tags in the recommendations.\n- Keep tags like <br> exactly as they are.\n- Return recommendations as a plain string with HTML tags preserved.\n\n## Part 3: Output Format\n\nReturn a JSON object with the following structure:\n\n{\n  \"summary\": \"<generated summary>\",\n  \"recommendations\": \"<generated recommendations with HTML tags preserved exactly (e.g., <br>)>\"\n}\n\n- Ensure that both fields are always present in the JSON.\n- Do NOT output raw filter strings, table data, or technical query language.\n- Keep both summary and recommendations concise and human-readable."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5920,
            "y": 7258
          }
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Return Payment Inquiry Analyst Result",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let data = $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_FOR_PAYMENT_INQUIRY_OBJECT_FETCH_LOOP.$output;\nlet sequence = 1;\nlet summary = $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_PAYMENT_INQUIRY_DATA_SUMMARIZER.$output;\nlet output = [];\n\n// 1) Summary block\noutput.push({\n  type: \"text\",\n  content: summary.summary.replace(/\\n/g,\n    \"<br>\"),\n  sequence: sequence++\n});\n\n// 2) Existing table/other blocks (add these first so the conditional text comes AFTER)\ndata.forEach((dataFetched) => {\n  try {\n    let toPush = JSON.parse(dataFetched).result;\n    if(toPush.content.length){\n      toPush.sequence = sequence++;\n      output.push(toPush);\n    }\n  } catch (e) {\n        // Do nothing if JSON.parse fails; output remains unchanged.\n    }\n});\n\n\nif (summary.recommendations != \"\") {\n    let updatedRecommendations = summary.recommendations +\n        \"<br>View Related Invoices<br>View Payment Processing Details\";\n\n    output.push({\n      type: \"text\",\n      content: updatedRecommendations.replace(/\\n/g, \"<br>\"),\n      sequence: sequence++\n    });\n}\n\nreturn output;"
          },
